,"rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The metadata declares a dependency on the external OpenHue CLI and a Homebrew install formula, which is disclosed and coherent with the skill purpose.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions are limited to setup, reading Hue resources, and user-directed light, brightness, color, and scene changes; no prompt overrides, unrelated actions, or hidden execution paths were present.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill itself defines no persistence, background services, or privilege escalation; OpenHue setup may create local bridge authorization state managed by the CLI.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is controlling Hue lights and scenes, and the documented read/write commands match that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want Codex to control your Hue lights through OpenHue. During setup you may need to authorize the Hue Bridge, and afterward agent-issued commands can turn lights on or off, change brightness/color, and activate scenes, so use room names or IDs carefully.","findings":null,"agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013566142}}}}}